window.docContents[108].resolve({"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--A-New--add--Rule":{"contents":"\n\nHere's another rule we can use for add:\n\ntheorem add_succ : ∀ n m : Nat, n + (succ m) = succ (n + m) := by\n  intro n m\n  rfl\n\n\nNow, let's use add_succ in a proof:\n\ntheorem add_one (n : Nat) : n + (succ zero) = succ n + zero := by\n  rewrite [add_succ]\n  rewrite [add_zero]\n  rewrite [add_zero]\n  rfl\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Basics: Functional Programming in Lean\u0009Proof by Rewriting","header":"2.4.5. A New  add  Rule","id":"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--A-New--add--Rule"}});